sargo SDHCI: real eMMC writes behind boot-arg sargo_rw=1

With the RAM overlay (0086) nothing iOS writes survives a reboot, so every
boot is a first boot: LaunchServices rebuilds its database each time and
SpringBoard waits ~30 min for it on one CPU. sargo_rw=1 sends writes to the
userdata partition: CMD24 for one block, CMD25 + Auto CMD12 for up to 128
KiB, through the same ADMA2 bounce buffer as the CMD18 reads. A request
completes only after Transfer Complete, DAT0 high and CMD13 back in TRAN
with no R1 error bits, and init switches the eMMC cache off (EXT_CSD 33), so
HFS journal ordering holds when power is cut. A partial sector is read and
merged. A write error in fast mode drops to 1-bit 25 MHz and retries once.
Without sargo_rw=1 nothing changes (RAM overlay). The sampler line shows
"wrote N MB" in this mode.

--- a/bsd/dev/sargo_sdhci.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sargo_sdhci.c
